<article class="env-corollary" id="A309">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A309">Corollary <span data-tag="A309">3.2.5.20</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small category and $\calF : \calC \rightarrow \mSet $ a fibrant object of $(\mSet )^{\calC }$. Let $S = \Nerve (\calC )$, and let $\phi : \sCoNerve [S^{op}] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ denote the counit map. Then the natural transformation $\alpha _{\calC }^{+}$ of Remark <a href="/tag/030C" data-tag="030C">3.2.5.16</a> induces a weak equivalence $\Nerve _{\calF }(\calC )^{op} \rightarrow (Un^{+}_{\phi } \calF ^{op})$ $($with respect to the Cartesian model structure on $(\Set ^{+}_{\Delta })_{/ S^{op}}$$)$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It suffices to show that $\alpha _{\calC }^{+}$ induces an isomorphism of right derived functors $R \Nerve _{\bullet }(\calC )^{op} \rightarrow R (Un^{+}_{\phi } \bullet ^{op})$, which follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0E67" data-tag="0E67">3.2.5.17</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>